  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ad496817cc2ac7b498b32f0fc2de6fb3, type: 3}
  m_Name: R1_08_WrensNote
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::JournalEntry
  title: A note from Wren
  pages:
  - bigIdea: '"The old ones didn''t build the engine to make power. They built it
      to keep the heart beating."'
    notes: If you're reading this, you've come further than I ever did. The Heart
      Engine sleeps in the hall below, and the Great Shard beyond it is cracking.
      I tried alone, years ago, and I couldn't move the cart an inch. It was never
      meant for one. You two can do what I couldn't. Everything you've learned out
      there, you'll need it all down here. I'll be waiting with the kettle on. -
      Wren
    lookCloser: "The roots need <color=#896923>42 kg\xB7m/s</color>. A Burst gives
      <color=#896923>15</color>. The ramp is 3 m tall...\nHow heavy would the cart
      need to be?"
    funFact: Wren's handwriting gets shakier toward the end of the page, as if written
      in a hurry.
    marginP1: We won't let you down.
    marginP2: Kettle on. Got it.
    diagram:
      show: 0
      objectLabel: 2 kg
      forces: []
      caption: 
    sketch: {fileID: 0}
  tip: Load the cart with ore, then one of you holds the chock open while the other
    sends it down the ramp.
  sketch: {fileID: 0}
  sketchCaption: 
